09, 7263319.562407371], \"beginning_balance\": [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, -716.2500000000002, -2865.000000000001, -6446.250000000002, -10286.700000000004, -14645.550000000005, -19522.800000000003, -25322.772000000004, -32968.188, -42459.048, -51949.908, -61440.768, -70931.628, -80422.488, -89913.348, -99404.208, -108895.068, -118385.928, -123951.15404125772, -134412.65968125773, -146815.45660125773, -161159.54480125773, -175503.63300125772, -189847.72120125772, -204191.80940125772, -218535.89760125772, -232879.98580125772, -247224.07400125772, -261568.1622012577, -275912.2504012577, 2359122.759464994, 2344037.879464994, 2327471.4158649943, 2309423.3686649944, -67747.43799999962, -85795.48519999962, -103843.53239999962, -121891.57959999962, -139939.62679999962, -157987.67399999962, -176035.72119999962, -194083.7683999996, 4474034.098089436, 4455308.3229494365, 4435227.091929437, 4413790.405029437, -81680.37995999958, -103117.06685999958, -124553.75375999958, -145990.4406599996, -167427.1275599996, -188863.8144599996, -210300.5013599996, -231737.1882599996, 5755359.489931729, 5733334.231371729, 5710131.829491729, 5685752.284291729, -93986.75083999896, -118366.29603999894, -142745.84123999893, -167125.38643999893, -191504.93163999892, -215884.4768399989, -240264.0220399989, -264643.5672399989, 6634993.04579043, 6610071.39234043, 6584065.52239043, 6556975.43594043, -105107.69630000088, -132197.7827500009, -159287.8692000009, -186377.9556500009, -213468.0421000009, -240558.1285500009, -267648.2150000009, -294738.3014500009]}}','Sky Healthy Food runs a pasteurized-egg factory in 6th of October City, Giza, so it already has the main raw material for this project: eggshell, which is about 93-95% natural calcium carbonate. The eggshell is a waste of the egg-breaking business, so it is entered in the study at zero cost (raw material “Eggshells (own plant)”). In reality, getting rid of it costs Sky Healthy Food about EUR 100,000 per annum; this saving is not counted in the study’s figures. The study looks at a new SKY-CAL plant that washes, separates the membrane, dries and micronizes the shell (D90 about 18 micron) into two calcium carbonate grades plus a membrane powder co-product, on a shared line of about 100-150 tons of powder a month (process flow by Dr. Mahmoud Emara, June 2026). Equipment is ordered, delivered, installed and tested between January and June 2027; operation and the first sales start in July 2027 (membrane powder in October 2027). The study covers seven years (2027-2033), is in Egyptian pounds, and treats the plant as a new business inside Sky. Sources: client documents (process flow, product data sheet, safety data sheet, progress report January 2026, Egyptian customs imports January-August 2026), market data (USD/EGP about 54 on 21 October 2026; Central Bank of Egypt lending rate 20%) and expert estimates where no quotation exists yet. Equipment cost, staffing, utilities, selling prices and the membrane price are estimates to be replaced by quotations and buyer feedback.','How to read this study. It is an initial feasibility study with seven years of monthly figures. The base case is deliberately realistic: six months from the start of the study to the first sales, full capacity entered in every year (the ramp-up is in the share of capacity sold), salaries 25% above the first estimate, yearly renewal capex on every asset instead of one big replacement, and no second production line. Money figures are in EGP. Because the plant is heavy on equipment, a large part of the value (the terminal value) comes from the years after 2033, so look at the payback and at the share of the terminal value in the valuation tiles as well as at the NPV.','What decides the result, and what to confirm next. In the first review, a 5-year Excel version, the project was close to break-even, so small changes decided the sign of the NPV. The three drivers are: (1) the price and volume Sky can really get for membrane powder; (2) firm equipment quotations (the equipment cost is an estimate including about 10% contingency); (3) how much premium Bio-Active powder export customers will take. Also to confirm: the real tons of eggshell per day from the pasteurization plant and what Sky earns or pays for the shell today; which product is sold (with membrane protein and an egg-allergen label, or without); moisture target (process flow below 1%, data sheet up to 3%, exporters ask 0.2%); and the dust-explosion protection (minimum ignition energy test, ASTM E2019). The What-if screen holds a saved downside case (sales -15% on the powders and -50% on membrane powder, higher raw material cost, slower collections).','egp',3);
